A1. This fellow is hot stuff. ~ SAT.N
A5. The bait the poor fish loses. ~ WAD
A8. A celebrity who played on the "Sidewalks of New York." ~ SMITH
A13. Who was the victim of the first surgical operation? ~ ADAM
A14. On what precious stone are figures engraved in relief? ~ CAMEO
A16. An urgent entreaty. ~ PLEA
A17. Something only two-fisted people can do. ~ BOX
A18. The visable part of any typewriter. ~ HOSIERY
A20. What disappears when the band plays The Star Spangled Banner? ~ LAP
A21. A pronoun. ~ HE
A22. This stuff is usually pretty soft. ~ PAD
A23. What would Miss America say if her bathing suit ripped ~ OH
A25. This is often missing on a second-hand car. ~ ENGINE
A28. This kind of thing is pretty smooth—and has a lot of polish. ~ GLOSSY
A31. Large trees. ~ OAKS
A32. What kind of people never die young? ~ OLD
A34. What is the tie that binds? ~ KNOT
A35. What is the turning point of most revolutions? ~ AXLE
A36. This keeps the school-girl complexion on the skin you love to touch. ~ CREAM
A38. Name a gang of under cover men. ~ KLAN
A40. This means nothing. ~ NIL
A41. Another name for a nut. (Slang.) ~ BUG
A42. What started the fad of reducing? ~ FAT
A43. What must a dentist do to fill his last cavity? ~ DIE
A44. Name something that makes a plumber forgetful. ~ TOOL
A46. This is slang for flattery—and flappers never get enough of it. ~ TAFFY
A48. This is often on the hip these days. ~ PINT
A49. What one and one becomes in a minister's arithmetic. ~ UNIT
A51. We wonder if the Quaker Miss who said this had to walk home. ~ NAY
A52. Lot's wife turned to rubber and then to salt when she was told to do this. ~ FLEE
A53. To attack with argument or abuse. ~ ASSAIL
A54. What composes the most famous attraction at Atlantic City? ~ BOARDS
A56. What do iron horses run around on? (Abbr.) ~ RR
A57. First name of a famous play producer. ~ SAM
A59. Indefinite article. ~ AN
A60. What did WE and MACHADO do at Havana? ~ MET
A63. What was Heflin overcome by in Washington? ~ EGOTISM
A66. What do promising young lawyers do when they go to court? ~ WOO
A68. What does John Roach Straton see everywhere through his colored glasses? ~ EVIL
A70. A proclamation or decree having the force of law ~ EDICT
A71. When you know a new day has arrived. ~ DAWN
A72. A good place to get off at. ~ DEPOT
A73. This has proved the downfall of many a king. ~ ACE
A74. Do things according to this man and you can't go wrong. ~ HOYLE

D1. What does a sugar daddy wrap his Baby Bunting in? ~ SABLE
D2. This is a bustle. ~ ADO
D3. This is the price of freedom to the bachelors of Italy. ~ TAX
D4. What comes each day before noon? (Init.) ~ .M
D5. This has a sting to it. ~ WASP
D6. What word describes Al's disposition? ~ AMIABLE
D7. An illustrous achievement. ~ DEED
D9. Army copper. (Init.) ~ MP
D10. The kind of wind Lindbergh—or anyone else— dislikes. ~ ILL
D11. What will the London bootlegger peddle when England goes dry? ~ TEA
D12. What will you be "No end" if you get "Here's How"? ~ HAPPY
D14. Any two is this in the school of love. ~ CO
D15. A conjunction which marks an alternative. ~ OR
D18. These are always laying around the place. ~ HENS
D19. This may be good but its always yellow. ~ YOLK
D21. To do this you must have two feet on the ground. ~ HIKE
D24. Any goose is apt to do this. ~ HONK
D26. What word means harmful; pernicious; deadly? ~ NOXIOUS
D27. The ocean has more of these than anyone can count. ~ GALLONS
D29. A man who is always up in arms. ~ SOLDIER
D30. What do reputations become at sewing circles? ~ STAINED
D32. This gets the air before it gives the air. ~ ORGAN
D33. Non compos mentis. ~ DAFFY
D35. This is as busy as a bee. ~ ANT
D36. What some folks do with old safety razor blades. ~ CUT
D37. What is the shortest month of the year. (Careful now.) ~ MAY
D39. This is a snare. ~ NET
D45. There is no truth in this. ~ LIAR
D47. What kind of person goes crazy over something? ~ FANATIC
D48. A scheme or project. ~ PLAN
D50. Name something that comes from a rubber plant. ~ TIRE
D52. This is frothy. ~ FOAM
D53. The best way to go to Chicago. ~ ARMED
D55. In what age did men have equal rights with women? ~ SIONE
D57. What a dyspeptic craves after every meal? ~ SODA
D58. What even anti-prohibitionists dislike having in the cellar. ~ MICE
D61. A fig leaf, a rib and a hank o' hair. ~ EVE
D62. What is a public secret at the races? ~ TIP
D64. A large clectrical manufacturing Co. (Abbr.) ~ GE
D65. This is hard to get over. (Abbr.) ~ ST
D66. A path or route. ~ WAY
D67. If this is so wise. why does it stay up all night? ~ OWL
D69. This word means lamp: get an eye-full; take in. ~ LO
D71. What word means to cheat or swindle? ~ DO


